00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:41.360
QUINN SLACK: Different
in a few ways.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.870
So your IDE is optimized
for editing code--

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:46.820
and usually, in one project.

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:49.760
And maybe 10, 20 years
ago, if you're a developer,

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.470
you could just be
working in one project.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:54.920
But these days, you have to use
so much open-source code or so

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:57.517
many other micro
services in your company,

00:06:57.517 --> 00:06:59.850
and the job of a developer
has just gotten a lot harder.

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.480
So we built a product
from the ground up

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.440
that actually understands
cross-repository references,

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.380
linkages.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:09.530
So you can point to
any piece of code.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:12.530
You can say, show me everywhere
in the open-source world--

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:15.410
or everywhere in my company--
this thing is being called.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.980
You can instantly search
across all your repositories--

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:22.014
hundreds or thousands of
repositories-- at any version.

00:07:22.014 --> 00:07:23.930
You don't need to wait
for them to be indexed.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:27.080
And so the tools that we
have as developers today--

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:31.610
I think they solve the problems
we had maybe 10 years ago.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:35.750
But with the explosion of
open source, micro services,

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:38.240
a lot more things, the job
has just gotten a lot harder.

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:41.060
And we're building the
tools to help developers

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.500
solve these problems today.

00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.416
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Cool.

00:07:43.416 --> 00:07:46.640
And that basically
is a web application

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.130
where people can browse
the code on everything,

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:51.849
