00:07:51.849 --> 00:07:52.640
QUINN SLACK: Right.

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:56.930
So you can get Sourcegraph
on the desktop,

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:58.640
and that is something
that you download.

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:01.026
And you can browse
all your local code.

00:08:01.026 --> 00:08:02.150
You can browse remote code.

00:08:02.150 --> 00:08:04.400
And it's a universal
code browser.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:07.670
It makes all the world's code
transparently available to you.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:09.860
And inside of
that, of course, we

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:11.360
have language
analyzers-- which we

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:14.360
call language servers-- built
on Microsoft's Language Server

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.070
Protocol, which is
the new standard.

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:17.690
It was released
about a year ago,

00:08:17.690 --> 00:08:20.310
and already you have
servers for most languages,

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:22.475
and it's a really
cool new standard.

00:08:22.475 --> 00:08:25.520
We have a lot of people work
on language servers internally,

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.070
and a lot of other people
at other companies and--

00:08:28.070 --> 00:08:30.000
then, yeah, you can
access it on the desktop.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.870
You can get it in our
Chrome extension on GitHub.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.258
So you can be viewing
code on GitHub.

00:08:35.258 --> 00:08:36.799
You can be looking
at a pull request,

00:08:36.799 --> 00:08:39.169
and you put your mouse over
any token, and you get a hover.

00:08:39.169 --> 00:08:40.294
You can do Find References.

00:08:40.294 --> 00:08:41.929
You can do Go To Definition.

00:08:41.929 --> 00:08:44.630
And you can get it integrated
into your own editor.

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.797
You can get it on the CLI, and
you can get it on a web app.

00:08:47.797 --> 00:08:49.130
FRANCESC CAMPOY: I really like--

